    "created_at": "2019-08-22T10:06:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-22T10:06:15Z",
    "body": "@annevk Are you saying that there are no privacy-sensitive aspects to the DOM that have changed recently?  Or that such a review has been done, but elsewhere?\r\n\r\nIn general, the request from PING is that, for functionality that has been recently added to the standard, can you answer the questions on the linked to security and privacy questionnaire.  [What new functionality has been provided to pages](https://www.w3.org/TR/security-privacy-questionnaire/#purpose), if the group [has considered whether a subset, or more privacy-preserving version of that functionality, would be sufficient, and if not, how the current level was selected](https://www.w3.org/TR/security-privacy-questionnaire/#minimum-data), etc.\r\n\r\nIf though, the issue is just choosing the \"changed since\" date for comparison, and thats whats not clear, I'm happy to make a suggestion, given the edit / revision history of the document, but maybe changes since the Memorandum of Understanding would be a good jumping off point.  WDYT?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
