    "updated_at": "2019-08-22T17:37:49Z",
    "body": "I'm saying that I'm not aware of anyone having done such a review, ever. Or if they have, no issues were filed as a result. No changes since the W3C MoU were privacy-relevant afaict.\r\n\r\nThe only somewhat problematic answer I can imagine is that for some primitives there's multiple ways to get to them, mostly due to how the web evolved. That's not really fixable. But then again, having `characterSet`, `inputEncoding`, and `charset` isn't really a privacy-problem. Ideally we wouldn't have them at all, but here we are.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
