    "created_at": "2019-09-08T00:18:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-08T00:18:01Z",
    "body": "Hi @annevk i see, this is all useful.  After re-reading the spec, and reminding myself whats in the HTML spec (which has lots of privacy relevant stuff, of course) and whats covered by the DOM spec, I see your point, that the privacy and security sections probably aren't needed (so this also applies to https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/776)\r\n\r\nOne last thing that'd be helpful for us though, in thinking through how to do future DOM reviews (since DOM and HTML are unique balls of wax re W3C), is there anything you could point us to / share with us about how the group thinks through the privacy and security aspects of the standard?  Do you have implicit guidelines, or firm rules, or anything like that that guides the group's work?\r\n\r\nThanks for working through this with us",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
